WEBVTT

00:09.650 --> 00:11.650
Welcome back, Theodora.

00:12.160 --> 00:13.900
Call me "Esta" here.

00:14.320 --> 00:17.270
Right. Sorry, I haven't 
gotten used to it yet.

00:41.220 --> 00:47.930
<b>Banished from the Hero's Party,
I Decided to Live a Quiet Life in the Countryside 2nd</b>

01:58.500 --> 02:03.510
<b>Zoltan's Solstice Festival</b>

01:59.050 --> 02:01.210
The previous demon lord's airship?

02:01.720 --> 02:04.930
It's the ship Ruti took to Zoltan.

02:05.770 --> 02:11.710
If Van heads to Zoltan and runs into Ruti,

02:11.710 --> 02:13.320
it will not be pretty.

02:14.070 --> 02:16.490
We need to avoid that, for Ruti's sake.

02:17.910 --> 02:20.550
Could you head to Zoltan for me?

02:21.000 --> 02:23.190
Red must be informed of these events.

02:23.630 --> 02:24.700
Very well.

02:25.990 --> 02:29.120
Is the new "hero" the real deal?

02:31.180 --> 02:35.840
The saint appraised him, and the Church's
 leadership have recognized him as such,

02:36.380 --> 02:38.420
so I would surmise that he must be...

02:39.110 --> 02:41.430
But he is nothing like Ruti.

02:42.430 --> 02:45.610
All we can do now is wait and see.

02:45.610 --> 02:50.230
I understand. I'll do what I can to help.

02:52.560 --> 02:54.060
Thank you, Albert.

02:54.790 --> 02:56.560
I'm glad you're here for me.

03:04.640 --> 03:05.450
Welcome.

03:05.880 --> 03:09.460
I'll take some of your new concoction.

03:09.870 --> 03:11.790
The dragonshroom essence?

03:11.790 --> 03:13.120
Yep, yep!

03:13.120 --> 03:15.420
That drink really gives 
you a burst of energy!

03:15.750 --> 03:20.340
It's not every day you visit so early, Nao.

03:20.570 --> 03:22.620
Today's festival day.

03:22.620 --> 03:25.550
If I waste any time, the day 
will be over before I know it.

03:27.140 --> 03:29.520
Let me throw in some for Mido and Gonz, too.

03:29.840 --> 03:31.310
Thanks, Red!

03:36.560 --> 03:37.690
That should do it.

03:38.570 --> 03:40.950
Are you ready to go, Rit?

03:41.140 --> 03:42.500
Coming!

03:49.540 --> 03:50.630
I'm here.

03:51.060 --> 03:52.160
How do I look?

03:52.910 --> 03:54.780
You look great.

03:55.360 --> 03:58.130
I love how you look in that coat, too!

03:59.790 --> 04:01.350
Shall we get going, then?

04:02.080 --> 04:04.340
Do you have what Zeff asked for?

04:04.730 --> 04:06.720
Got it right here.

04:06.720 --> 04:08.350
Let's go, then.

04:13.350 --> 04:17.460
Wow... Talk about the festival spirit.

04:17.460 --> 04:21.040
<i>Today's the Drake Rider and 
Saint Licinius's Solstice Festival,</i>

04:21.040 --> 04:23.760
<i>based on an Avalonian legend.</i>

04:24.460 --> 04:27.440
<i>Even the Zoltanians, who tend 
to laze around during the day,</i>

04:27.440 --> 04:30.360
<i>are out living it up from the 
morning on this special day.</i>

04:30.360 --> 04:32.450
Hey, Red!

04:35.750 --> 04:37.630
You having fun?

04:37.630 --> 04:40.840
Hey, Gonz. Looks like you're in a good mood.

04:41.040 --> 04:43.980
Of course. It's a festival.

04:43.980 --> 04:46.830
Everyone's off work. And...

04:51.210 --> 04:53.680
I'm taking tomorrow off for the hangover.

04:53.680 --> 04:55.720
Tomorrow, too?

04:55.720 --> 04:59.020
Who goes to work the day after a party?

04:59.310 --> 05:02.030
You tell them, Gonz! What a man's man!

05:02.210 --> 05:07.030
No... Even Tanta's going to 
grow up to be a good-for-nothing.

05:07.860 --> 05:08.700
Tanta.

05:08.700 --> 05:10.490
What is it, Red?

05:11.180 --> 05:14.000
I'm going to be back on the job tomorrow.

05:14.000 --> 05:16.670
C'mon, just take the day off.

05:16.670 --> 05:18.080
I mean, look at that.

05:22.780 --> 05:28.220
This is how the Drake Rider and Saint Licinius's 
Solstice Festival goes in Zoltan, huh?

05:28.220 --> 05:30.390
Is it different where you're from, Rit?

05:30.870 --> 05:33.990
Yeah. It was a lot more 
formal back in Loggarvia.

05:33.990 --> 05:35.290
Huh...

05:36.830 --> 05:42.410
The objective is the same—the Drake Rider 
and Saint repelling the winter demon—

05:42.410 --> 05:45.710
but it's great how different 
regions do it differently.

05:45.710 --> 05:50.910
Here, we sing, dance, and party with all 
our hearts to chase the winter demon away.

05:51.390 --> 05:53.280
That's the Zoltan way.

05:53.280 --> 05:55.750
It really does a number on you.

05:55.750 --> 05:59.430
That's why I gotta take tomorrow off.

06:00.200 --> 06:01.630
That makes sense.

06:02.240 --> 06:03.940
Let's take the day off.

06:03.940 --> 06:05.090
Rit...

06:05.410 --> 06:07.270
Take the day off!

06:07.380 --> 06:09.000
Take the day off!

06:09.110 --> 06:10.880
Take the day off!

06:10.980 --> 06:12.570
Take the day off!

06:12.670 --> 06:13.640
Take the day off!

06:13.640 --> 06:15.630
Fine, I get it.

06:15.630 --> 06:18.830
I bet all of Zoltan will be out of 
commission tomorrow anyway.

06:18.830 --> 06:20.730
Guess we can take it easy.

06:21.890 --> 06:23.810
Yay!

06:23.810 --> 06:25.230
Yay.

06:26.450 --> 06:28.150
We'll take the day off, too.

06:28.150 --> 06:29.280
Uh...

06:29.870 --> 06:30.740
Okay.

06:33.030 --> 06:38.080
How could this be? Ruti and Tisse 
grew up to be good-for-nothings, too.

06:38.670 --> 06:39.880
Isn't this fun?

06:41.040 --> 06:42.520
I guess it's okay.

06:50.060 --> 06:52.420
This soothes the soul.

06:52.420 --> 06:53.800
I guess...

06:54.920 --> 06:56.350
Oparara?

06:56.350 --> 06:58.600
Are you done already?

06:58.600 --> 07:00.180
L-Like hell I am!

07:00.180 --> 07:02.420
If that's a joke, it ain't funny, Megria!

07:02.420 --> 07:04.940
I'm just gettin' started here!

07:04.940 --> 07:07.570
Oh, that's good to hear.

07:08.090 --> 07:08.700
Hup.

07:09.260 --> 07:10.950
Ack!

07:14.720 --> 07:16.580
That smells great.

07:27.590 --> 07:29.180
Are you all right?

07:29.180 --> 07:30.380
Thanks, I needed a drink.

07:36.760 --> 07:38.880
Do you two have the day off?

07:38.880 --> 07:41.270
Yes. Well, the Adventurers' Guild does, at least.

07:42.260 --> 07:43.310
Meanwhile...

07:44.180 --> 07:48.130
I'll be taking my cart out like always.

07:48.580 --> 07:53.920
My oden's busy gettin' real 
tasty in the pot right now,

07:55.920 --> 07:59.260
so I came here to sweat out and detox.

07:59.260 --> 08:00.200
I know what you mean.

08:00.780 --> 08:04.530
Oden can taste entirely different 
based on how long it's cooked.

08:04.530 --> 08:05.560
Hold it, kid!

08:05.560 --> 08:08.340
Let me go! I didn't do anything wrong!

08:09.580 --> 08:12.430
Did you not see me standing right here?

08:12.430 --> 08:14.870
Like hell you were! Quit lying!

08:14.870 --> 08:15.850
Say what?

08:15.850 --> 08:16.570
Hmph!

08:17.320 --> 08:18.760
What's wrong?

08:19.430 --> 08:21.420
This kid cut in line.

08:21.420 --> 08:23.480
I-I was there first!

08:23.480 --> 08:25.690
You're the one who cut in line!

08:25.690 --> 08:28.630
Huh? What was that, you shrimp?

08:29.450 --> 08:31.030
Don't you mock me!

08:39.800 --> 08:41.010
Ademi...

08:41.010 --> 08:42.660
Don't do that. You could've hurt him.

08:48.140 --> 08:50.850
I apologize for the trouble.

08:52.670 --> 08:57.410
His Blessing awakened recently, 
so he's still a little unstable.

08:57.410 --> 08:58.770
You apologize, too.

08:59.820 --> 09:00.970
I'm sorry!

09:01.520 --> 09:05.130
Don't be. I got a little worked up, too.

09:05.760 --> 09:08.730
You can't be blamed for 
your Blessing's impulses.

09:09.340 --> 09:12.990
<i>"Can't be blamed for your 
Blessing's impulses," huh?</i>

09:14.400 --> 09:16.820
Ademi's grown up to be a fine young man.

09:17.400 --> 09:18.270
Yeah.

09:18.640 --> 09:20.280
Red!

09:20.630 --> 09:23.160
Everyone!

09:23.760 --> 09:26.060
I see something bouncing around over there.

09:27.600 --> 09:28.920
Hey!

09:28.170 --> 09:28.920
Over here!

09:29.180 --> 09:30.470
Yarandrala!

09:30.470 --> 09:32.300
Rit!

09:34.560 --> 09:36.550
The town's really livened up today, huh?

09:38.140 --> 09:39.950
Glad you're enjoying yourself.

09:39.950 --> 09:42.810
There are so many stalls 
I've never seen before.

09:42.810 --> 09:43.920
Look!

09:43.920 --> 09:47.770
They said this sacred mask was 
made by a legendary great sage!

09:48.150 --> 09:51.740
Uh, Yarandrala? How old are you, again?

09:52.150 --> 09:52.770
Hm...

09:53.560 --> 09:57.360
Some might see me as a 
young lass of around 50!

09:58.300 --> 10:00.940
An elf joke... That's a new one.

10:06.280 --> 10:07.520
Come one, come all!

10:14.670 --> 10:16.370
Hey, bossman!

10:16.370 --> 10:19.190
You never told me you knew a Kiramin elf!

10:19.190 --> 10:20.510
A Kiramin elf?

10:20.510 --> 10:25.020
We elves refer to one another 
by the place we were born.

10:25.020 --> 10:27.390
So that makes me a Zoltan elf.

10:27.390 --> 10:29.730
I'm amazed you can tell where she's from.

10:29.730 --> 10:31.830
We just kinda know.

10:31.830 --> 10:35.750
Even among high elves, 
Kiramin elves are special.

10:35.750 --> 10:39.510
How is a country bumpkin like 
me supposed to talk to her?

10:39.510 --> 10:41.950
There are alarm bells going off in my head!

10:41.950 --> 10:43.330
Oparara?

10:43.330 --> 10:44.720
Y-Yes, ma'am!

10:44.720 --> 10:49.980
I certainly am from Kiramin, 
but that doesn't mean anything.

10:51.360 --> 10:52.390
It's okay.

10:52.860 --> 10:55.500
Yarandrala's my friend,

10:56.040 --> 10:58.090
so don't worry about all that.

10:59.640 --> 11:00.840
Ruti!

11:01.170 --> 11:05.350
Anyway, can I have some oden? I'm starving.

11:06.480 --> 11:08.190
You betcha!

11:08.190 --> 11:10.160
What will it be?

11:10.160 --> 11:11.850
I've got some fresh octopus today.

11:12.180 --> 11:13.660
The fish balls have my seal of approval, too!

11:13.660 --> 11:17.000
I'll have some, then. And some burdock.

11:17.000 --> 11:18.860
I'll have the octopus and some egg.

11:19.440 --> 11:21.850
I'll have the same as Ms. Ruti.

11:21.850 --> 11:24.370
And four fish paste grills, please.

11:24.670 --> 11:26.490
Uh, as for me...

11:26.490 --> 11:28.740
I'll have the octopus, 
egg, burdock, fish balls,

11:28.740 --> 11:30.930
squid balls, radish, and beef tendon.

11:30.930 --> 11:35.030
And also fish cake, seaweed, jelly strings...

11:35.030 --> 11:36.340
And a cake pouch!

11:36.340 --> 11:37.900
That's a pretty big order.

11:38.790 --> 11:41.070
It all just sounded so good.

11:41.070 --> 11:42.760
How about you, Yarandrala?

11:42.990 --> 11:46.410
Hm... I'll have what you're having.

11:46.410 --> 11:50.270
Octopus and burdock. 
And add some fish balls, please.

11:51.740 --> 11:52.550
Right away!

11:53.760 --> 11:54.860
Here you are!

11:55.500 --> 11:57.360
Let's eat!

11:57.870 --> 12:00.380
Add this here and it'll taste twice as good!

12:01.370 --> 12:04.490
Hey, we didn't order something so expensive.

12:04.930 --> 12:07.020
It's from the lady over here.

12:07.460 --> 12:08.840
Ruti?!

12:08.840 --> 12:09.490
Yep.

12:10.000 --> 12:14.250
Wait, wait. I can't let my 
little sister pay for me.

12:14.720 --> 12:18.080
I happen to be a hotshot 
B-ranked adventurer, you know?

12:18.080 --> 12:21.670
And guess who just got paid.

12:21.670 --> 12:23.260
What's in that bag?

12:23.520 --> 12:26.580
You told me to live as I wanted.

12:26.580 --> 12:30.660
And right now, I want you all 
to enjoy some yummy oden.

12:32.710 --> 12:35.900
You're both sharing that money, right? 
Stop her or she'll use all of it.

12:36.720 --> 12:39.190
What she decides goes.

12:51.340 --> 12:54.210
Okay, I'll help myself, Ruti.

12:54.210 --> 12:55.000
Good.

13:11.570 --> 13:12.250
Ack!

13:12.250 --> 13:12.970
Oh!

13:16.080 --> 13:19.900
No need to run. 
You're Zoltan's representative.

13:19.900 --> 13:21.610
Act like it!

13:21.610 --> 13:23.180
Ouch!

13:23.660 --> 13:25.070
What kind of representative is he?

13:25.640 --> 13:28.150
When we visited the zoogs,

13:28.150 --> 13:31.490
the elder said they were having 
trouble due to a lack of trade.

13:31.490 --> 13:32.580
Huh...

13:33.440 --> 13:35.750
Godwin will be handling that from now on.

13:37.990 --> 13:41.040
I owe ya big-time, Red.

13:41.040 --> 13:44.430
And he'd be fine even if he ran 
into monsters on the way there.

13:44.430 --> 13:46.420
Can this guy really be trusted?

13:47.330 --> 13:49.180
Of course I can! Trust is my middle name!

13:49.500 --> 13:52.120
He's got the skills, at least.

13:52.120 --> 13:55.870
You'd better work hard to 
make up for what you did.

13:57.830 --> 14:00.210
Looks like it's time for the grand finale.

14:00.210 --> 14:01.190
Let's go!

14:10.560 --> 14:11.370
Gah!

14:11.850 --> 14:16.170
Follow the script and go down already!

14:17.550 --> 14:18.250
Oh?

14:18.250 --> 14:19.250
Is that you,

14:19.250 --> 14:21.560
my beloved lady warrior?!

14:21.560 --> 14:22.370
Who's that?

14:22.370 --> 14:23.250
No idea.

14:23.250 --> 14:25.840
Gah! I can't see her!

14:26.290 --> 14:27.790
He's staring at you, though.

14:30.880 --> 14:35.220
He's the guy you threw off the 
bridge on the way to Zoltan.

14:35.220 --> 14:35.840
Oh.

14:38.370 --> 14:39.480
Don't remember.

14:41.160 --> 14:43.190
My name is Otto!

14:43.190 --> 14:44.230
Please remember it we—

14:45.540 --> 14:46.280
Huh?

14:47.560 --> 14:50.070
Is that you, Danan?

14:53.760 --> 14:55.120
Heya, Red.

14:55.120 --> 14:57.360
It's been too long, Danan!

14:57.360 --> 15:00.210
Hey. I hear you'll be staying 
in Zoltan for a while.

15:01.180 --> 15:03.040
What happened to your arm?

15:03.040 --> 15:04.380
It's not a big deal.

15:04.720 --> 15:06.400
It looks like a big deal!

15:07.110 --> 15:08.420
Are you okay?

15:08.420 --> 15:10.020
I'm fine.

15:10.020 --> 15:12.680
I wanted to head out already,

15:12.680 --> 15:15.010
but the doc kept nagging 
me about staying put.

15:15.470 --> 15:17.120
So much for that!

15:17.120 --> 15:19.160
This counts as staying put for me.

15:22.940 --> 15:25.940
Cursed winter demon! Where did it go?!

15:26.180 --> 15:29.530
Whoops, gotta play my role till the end.

15:58.640 --> 16:01.440
Man, I wish there was a way 
to make some easy money.

16:01.440 --> 16:04.140
Maybe if there was some 
hidden treasure in Zoltan.

16:04.140 --> 16:05.290
Right?

16:05.290 --> 16:08.820
Like an airship or something!

16:09.120 --> 16:11.390
In your dreams.

16:11.390 --> 16:12.760
D'aww.

16:31.750 --> 16:32.800
Big Brother.

16:33.550 --> 16:36.430
Thanks for today. I had lots of fun.

16:38.210 --> 16:40.340
Really? Glad to hear it.

16:43.540 --> 16:46.320
But there's still something we haven't done.

16:49.870 --> 16:51.340
Shall we dance?

16:51.790 --> 16:54.070
Me? Dance with you?

16:56.390 --> 16:57.020
Okay.

16:58.020 --> 17:03.510
But the last time I danced was 
before you became a knight.

17:04.390 --> 17:06.490
I won't be good at it.

17:06.490 --> 17:08.590
It's not about how good you are at it.

17:09.360 --> 17:11.380
It's how much fun you have dancing.

17:11.990 --> 17:12.710
Now, come.

17:17.780 --> 17:18.570
Okay.

17:21.930 --> 17:23.200
Is this okay?

17:23.830 --> 17:24.640
What's up?

17:25.740 --> 17:30.400
Am I really allowed to feel this happy?

17:32.630 --> 17:34.110
I say it's fine.

17:35.550 --> 17:41.080
You've endured so much pain 
to make others happy.

17:41.950 --> 17:46.080
I think it's about time 
you let yourself feel happy.

17:46.830 --> 17:47.990
Big Brother...

17:49.170 --> 17:50.370
Thank you.

17:59.620 --> 18:01.160
Would you like some wine?

18:01.160 --> 18:02.350
No, I'm quite all right.

18:03.710 --> 18:06.350
How is Van in your eyes?

18:06.690 --> 18:09.100
He goes beyond my expectations in many ways.

18:09.750 --> 18:11.060
Is that so?

18:11.760 --> 18:14.450
Looking at the records you gave me,

18:14.450 --> 18:16.920
he is growing at an unbelievable pace.

18:16.920 --> 18:22.080
But that only makes sending him to 
Zoltan seem like a waste of time.

18:22.890 --> 18:25.040
Have you been to Zoltan?

18:25.380 --> 18:27.700
Only briefly.

18:27.700 --> 18:30.740
That land has no economic 
or historical significance.

18:30.740 --> 18:32.040
It has nothing.

18:32.370 --> 18:35.860
Even if the demon lord's airship is there,

18:35.860 --> 18:37.970
what purpose would it serve for Van?

18:38.290 --> 18:41.970
We need to ascertain that, which is 
why information is of the essence.

18:44.110 --> 18:48.870
Should the airship be found, 
I'm sure we will require your help.

18:52.700 --> 18:54.980
I'll be counting on you,

18:55.440 --> 18:56.800
Escarlata.

19:02.640 --> 19:04.880
The festival's over...

19:04.880 --> 19:06.620
It'll be back next year.

19:07.150 --> 19:08.870
Will we see it together next year?

19:09.280 --> 19:10.370
Of course.

19:10.960 --> 19:12.380
And the year after that?

19:13.020 --> 19:13.880
Still together.

19:29.570 --> 19:30.640
What's that?

19:31.410 --> 19:32.430
A gift for you.

19:36.130 --> 19:36.820
Wait...

19:37.360 --> 19:42.170
Well, you know, I couldn't 
get you that blue sapphire,

19:42.170 --> 19:46.720
but this is my way of promising you 
I'll get you that ring someday.

19:46.720 --> 19:48.900
So, it's an engagement necklace?

19:48.900 --> 19:49.520
Yeah.

19:50.050 --> 19:50.710
Here.

19:51.570 --> 19:52.460
Put it on for me.

19:52.870 --> 19:54.210
S-Sure.

20:01.440 --> 20:02.870
How does it look?

20:04.410 --> 20:05.180
It looks great.

20:06.460 --> 20:07.180
You're beautiful.

20:10.400 --> 20:11.510
Sheesh!

20:13.870 --> 20:15.250
This is no fair!

20:15.250 --> 20:15.900
Rit?

20:16.470 --> 20:21.840
You tell me to wait for a ring 
but get me something so pretty?

20:21.840 --> 20:24.290
That's no fair! I love you!

20:25.810 --> 20:31.290
You'd better take responsibility for 
drawing all this love out of me.

20:32.460 --> 20:33.470
How would you have me do that?

20:34.410 --> 20:35.420
You and I...

20:37.010 --> 20:39.920
We'll sleep in tomorrow.

20:42.140 --> 20:43.590
You're no fair yourself.

20:54.030 --> 20:57.170
There's no information 
about the airship anywhere.

20:57.700 --> 20:59.230
Maybe we need to go harder.

20:59.660 --> 21:03.270
Don't. Causing a ruckus will only 
make it harder for us to make a move.

21:07.690 --> 21:08.660
It's you!

21:09.660 --> 21:10.600
Run!

21:13.700 --> 21:14.620
Mr. Crawly Wawly.

21:18.910 --> 21:21.710
Wh-What's Tisse doing here?!

21:21.710 --> 21:24.220
Something must be going on here in Zoltan.

21:27.870 --> 21:29.530
What the heck is all this?!

21:40.820 --> 21:42.120
Oh, crap.

21:55.110 --> 21:56.080
Are you...
